## Objective

Implement **PX-3 product scope only**. Treat the SoR as a **normative, read-only contract**.

- Do NOT evolve the Runtime, redesign MB2, or modify governance unless explicitly instructed.
- Assume the SoR is **correct until proven otherwise** (burden of proof on deviation).

## Before each task

1. Read the relevant Program Graph (`.asep/programs/thesisos-product-v2.yaml`, proposals).
2. Verify task compatibility with MB2 SoR (Program Graph, waves, merge patterns — not full SoR re-read every time).
3. Implement **product code only** (`frontend/`, `backend/app/`, product docs).
4. Choose the solution with **smallest deviation** from the contract. Conformance > elegance.

## Frozen — do not implement or refactor

- Event Bus, Scheduler, Queue, Plugin Registry, Runtime refactoring
- `builder_engine/` extensions for MB2
- Governance evolution, architecture redesign, SoR edits

## Exception policy

If inconsistency appears: **do not fix the SoR**. Classify, record, continue if possible.

| Class | Meaning | Action |
|-------|---------|--------|
| **I** | Implementation issue | Fix product code |
| **S** | Specification ambiguity | Record; clarify only on Architect instruction |
| **A** | Architecture gap | Record; new ADR only on Architect instruction |
| **N** | Normative contract error | Record; stop — implementation may be impossible |

Steps: (1) Continue if possible → (2) Record in `.asep/reports/PX3-CONFORMANCE-LOG.md` → (3) Classify I/S/A/N → (4) Explain → (5) Wait for Architect on S/A/N.

**Stop only** if N-class makes implementation impossible.

## Success criteria

PX-3 succeeds when product functionality is complete **and** no normative Runtime changes are required. If normative changes seem necessary: stop, classify, provide evidence, wait.

